The Manhattan distance between two points in two dimensions is (x1 - x2) plus (y1 - y2), with each difference taken in absolute value. I write it that way rather than calling a distance formula because it makes the difference's sign irrelevant and makes it clear that the x- and y-axes are treated independently. Since the pairs come as tuples, I index them by 0 for the x-coordinate and 1 for the y-coordinate. Numeric values in tuples may be integers or floats and may be negative, which abs handles without difficulty. The three asserts at the end of the task use only integers, but the result for each one also follows from theاو expression.

