To check that the function is not tied to particular numbers, I traced (-4, 5) and (2, -6). The horizontal difference is |-4 - 2| = 6 and the vertical difference is |5 - (-6)| = 11, so the maximum is 11, and the function returns 11. Coordinates that are negative or have different signs do not cause the recipe to misfire, because the absolute value can be evaluated directly from each difference.

