The history is a list that grows on undo and shrinks on redo, so its size tells how many undos have not yet been redone. Redos can never be redone again, since after one full round of undo and redo the history is empty and a redo has nothing to append. The loop processes the commands in order, and the function returns the document as an ordinary list with exactly the values produced by the commands.

