The implementation uses a helper that computes the signed area of the triangle formed by a vertex, its predecessor, and its successor, so it needs only (x - x) * (y - y) and (y - y) * (x - x), and no explicit counters for directions or for lines meeting at a corner. It returns False for every strictly concave polygon and True for the convex ones listed in the asserts.

