The last assert needs special treatment, because zero minutes would otherwise reduce to an empty string. After that, splitting by sixty gives hours as the whole division and remaining minutes as the remainder. Each nonzero piece is written with its unit and an empty one is skipped, so exactly one hour with no leftover minutes becomes "2h", exactly seven minutes becomes "7m", and seven minutes after an hour becomes "1h7m". An input of zero uses the explicit '0m' branch.

